  "worked_solution": "The local truncation error (LTE) is the error made in a *single step* of a numerical method, when the step begins from an *exact value*. The LTE of a numerical method at step $n$ from $x$ with exact value ${y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)$ to ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{τ}_{n} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}})-{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}})-({y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)+Δy).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the LTE at each step, rounding to three decimal places in each case:\n\n- After the first step, we have ${x}_{\\text{new}}=0.19$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}=1.052.$ So, the LTE of the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{τ}_{1} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}(0.19)-1.052 \\\\  & ={e}^{0.3\\cdot 0.19}-1.052 \\\\  & ≈0.007.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- After the second step, we have ${x}_{\\text{new}}=0.38$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}=1.123.$ So, the LTE of the second step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{τ}_{2} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}(0.38)-1.123 \\\\  & ={e}^{0.3\\cdot 0.38}-1.123 \\\\  & ≈-0.002.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- After the third step, we have ${x}_{\\text{new}}=0.57$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}=1.181.$ So, the LTE of the third step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{τ}_{3} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}(0.57)-1.181 \\\\  & ={e}^{0.3\\cdot 0.57}-1.181 \\\\  & ≈0.005.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed table is as given below.\n\n| $n$ | $x$ | $y$ | ${τ}_{n}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $1.000$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $0.19$ | $1.052$ | $0.007$ |\n| $2$ | $0.38$ | $1.123$ | $-0.002$ |\n| $3$ | $0.57$ | $1.181$ | $0.005$ |",
